  "Question": "If \\(a+1\\) \\(=b+2\\) \\(=c+3\\) \\(=d+4\\) \\(=a+b+c+d+5,\\) then \\(a+b+c+d\\) is",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-5\\)",
    "B": "\\(-\\dfrac{10}{3}\\)",
    "C": "\\(-\\dfrac{7}{3}\\)",
    "D": "\\(\\dfrac{5}{3}\\)",
    "E": "\\(5\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Because only the sum is requested, let \\(S=a+b+c+d\\). Each of the four expressions \\(a+1\\), \\(b+2\\), \\(c+3\\), and \\(d+4\\) equals \\(S+5\\).\n\nAdding these four equalities removes the need to find the individual variables. The left sides sum to \\(S+10\\), and the right sides sum to \\(4S+20\\), so\n\\[\nS+10=4S+20.\n\\]\nSubtracting \\(S+20\\) from both sides gives \\(3S=-10\\). Therefore\n\\[\na+b+c+d=S=\\boxed{-\\frac{10}{3}},\n\\]\nwhich is choice B.",
